exercises.context:
You are preparing a briefing note in English for the board of a French industrial group with a large subsidiary in Nordavia, a fictional country with its own currency. The Central Bank of Nordavia (CBN) has a single mandate of price stability and an inflation target of 2%.

Latest data (hypotheses for this exercise):
- headline CPI inflation over the past 12 months: 5.2%;
- core inflation (excluding energy and food): 4.1%;
- CBN policy rate: 3.5%;
- real GDP growth over the past year: 0.3%;
- estimated output gap: −1% of potential GDP;
- the CBN's estimate of the neutral real interest rate (r*): 1%.

Analysts are split. Some argue that the CBN is "behind the curve" and must keep hiking; others fear that further hikes will push the economy into recession, especially as the government has just announced a fiscal consolidation plan (spending cuts and tax increases) to reduce its deficit.
